from pathlib import Path
import json
R=Path(__file__).parent

def main():
 s=json.loads((R/'results/summary.json').read_text());f=json.loads((R/'results/fresh-test-evaluation.json').read_text());d=json.loads((R/'results/learning.json').read_text());lines=['## Completed result','', 'The standalone recurrent model in experiment30 failed autonomous rollout (combined validation objective2.302 versus snapshot0.0728, about31.6x worse), despite teacher-forced next-step objective0.0654. This is evidence of rollout failure, not successful sequence learning. Stage31 therefore tested a separately disclosed hybrid snapshot-plus-recurrent-correction model.','', 'Fresh predictions and trained models were frozen before the two test FDS jobs were submitted. All frozen hashes were rechecked before evaluation. No FDS state is fed into prediction. Both test cases completed180s.','', '| Fresh case | Model | Hot-region MAE °C | HRR curve relative L1 | Radiation-dose relative L1 | Peak error °C |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in f['rows']:
  q=r['post_source'];lines.append(f"| {r['case']} | {r['model']} | {q['hot_MAE_C']:.1f} | {q['HRR_curve_relative_L1']:.3f} | {q['radiation_dose_relative_L1']:.3f} | {q['peak_error_C']:.1f} |")
 lines+=['','FDS output timestamps are slightly irregular: reference fields were linearly interpolated onto the frozen2s prediction times, with maximum nearest-frame offsets0.175s and0.074s. Predictions were unchanged, and no extrapolation was used. Metrics above cover source-off times>=22s. Hot-region error uses cells where either truth or prediction exceeds50°C. Radiation is integrated gas radiation intensity, not incident wall heat flux. Full-volume heat-release history and spatial radiation-dose errors are dimensionless;1.0 means100% relative L1 error. The report also contains airflow and flame-region overlap (HRRPUV>10kW/m³), not a visual flame label.','',f"Snapshot training took{d['snapshot_training']['fit_seconds']:.1f}s and hybrid training{d['hybrid_training']['fit_seconds']:.1f}s on an L4. Median inference for91 frames/180s was{s['inference_median_s']['snapshot']:.3f}s snapshot and{s['inference_median_s']['hybrid']:.3f}s hybrid on that GPU, excluding output transfer/rendering; this is not laptop CPU timing.",'','The hybrid uses the snapshot prediction at each requested time and a bounded learned correction. It is not a standalone physics solver. Its2m internal state predicts0.5m output fields. State-reset ablation removes persistent predicted state and latent memory; it is an ablation of the trained hybrid, not an independently retrained architecture. Snapshot and hybrid training budgets differ.','', 'Only two fresh configurations, one generic cone family, crown heights6/8/10m, diameter3m, fixed0.12moisture, two forcing profiles, loading0.8/1.2. Frozen particle geometry;0.5mFDS cells;20s artificial1500°C source; no trunks, buildings, combustible ground or embers. Taller crowns reduce top-boundary clearance. Agreement is against this fixed FDS setup, not physical validation.','',f"Stage31 reserved${s['budget_reservations_usd']:.2f} of its$2.50 cap; combined with Stage30's$1 reservation the total is${1+s['budget_reservations_usd']:.2f} under the$3.50 ceiling. Reservations are conservative limits, not invoice spend. GPU and CPU cleanup is verified separately in the retained job reports.",'', 'Animations: results/v31_04-comparison.gif and results/v31_11-comparison.gif. They show maximum-through-y projected gas temperature and heat-release density with fixed shared nonlinear scales; peaks may be clipped. They are field visualizations, not Smokeview flame/smoke rendering. Histories: results/fresh-histories.png.']
 p=R/'README.md';old=p.read_text().split('## Completed result')[0];p.write_text(old+'\n'+'\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
